# Target C: collar-to-augmented-defect budget

**Scope audit, 2026-10-04:** the endpoint specialization with
`x_B=O(sqrt(D))`, `t_D<=1.860+o(1)` has no unbounded canonical Type-II
survivor. The conditional finite collar/augmented-cell inequalities are
retained. See the [exact hull-side capacity audit](../docs/reports/target_c_hull_side_exact_train_capacity_audit_2026-10-04.md).

Date: 2026-10-03
Base main: f6f2c5d80ee30ca2c949f08b089b5ef606b1916c
Status: proof-only candidate, noncanonical. C-II and Level I remain open.

This note is independent of the current open-cell cut-divergence route. It couples the
high-t boundary-rhombus collar to canonical Section 123.

Let S=N_4^partial be the selected strict boundary-rhombus count from
target_c_high_t_boundary_rhombus_floor_2026-10-02.md. For an unloaded harmonic
component I_r use Section-123 notation A_r, a_r=|A_r|, T_r for triangular bounded
faces of J_r^+, Q_r^+=sum_(deg f>=5)(deg f-4), and d_tile for the global attachment
tiling deficit. Put k=d_H+s_Z.

Section 123 gives the exact identity

    2(e_BB-k) = sum_r(a_r-T_r+Q_r^+) + 2 d_tile.             (1)

## Lemma: every collar side is a nontriangular added polygon side

Fix a selected collar rhombus with cyclic boundary

    p - p' - z' - z - p.                                   (2)

The collar theorem gives that p,p' are consecutive loaded force-hull vertices,
z,z' are unloaded, pz and p'z' are attachment contacts, and zz' is an
unloaded-unloaded contact. Thus z,z' lie in one unloaded component I_r and
p,p' belong to A_r. Since p,p' are consecutive on the full loaded hull, they are
consecutive in the cyclic order of the subset A_r, so pp' is a side of P_r=conv(A_r).

In the Section-123 graph J_r^+, loaded-loaded contacts are omitted at first and every
side of P_r is then added. Therefore pp' is one of the added polygon sides. The other
three edges in (2) are already present. Because (2) is an actual bounded strict
rhombus face of the positive-contact core, its interior has no core vertex or contact
edge. Other added polygon sides lie on the boundary of P_r and cannot enter its
interior. Hence the bounded J_r^+ face incident with pp' is exactly the quadrilateral
(2), not a triangle.

Distinct selected collar rhombi have distinct loaded hull sides. If S_r are assigned
to I_r through their inner edge zz', then

    S_r <= a_r-T_r.                                         (3)

Summing,

    S <= sum_r(a_r-T_r).                                    (4)

## Exact budget

Combining (1) and (4) gives

    S + sum_r Q_r^+ + 2 d_tile <= 2(e_BB-k).                (5)

This is the new finite inequality.

Section 123 also gives P_exc,r<=5Q_r^+ for the actual induced harmonic graph. Hence

    sum_r P_exc,r
      <= 10(e_BB-k) - 5S - 10 d_tile.                       (6)

Thus the collar and harmonic exceptional-face perimeter do not have independent
linear allowances.

## Current high-t specialization

The high-t collar branch is full-core Type II. The promoted loaded-chord theorem gives
c_B=0 and e_BB=q-m, where m is the number of nonunit loaded-hull sides. With
t_D=(q-k)/D,

    e_BB-k = t_D D-m.                                       (7)

Therefore

    S + sum_r Q_r^+ + 2 d_tile <= 2t_D D-2m.               (8)

The current collar theorem gives

    S >= 4 per(F)-6t_D D-6nu-9x_B-8.                       (9)

Consequently

    sum_r Q_r^+ + 2 d_tile
      <= 8t_D D-4 per(F)+6nu+9x_B+8-2m.                    (10)

In the square-root branch nu=O(sqrt(D)), x_B=O(sqrt(D)), and per(F)/D->pi.
Along t_D->t,

    limsup (sum_r Q_r^+ + 2d_tile)/D <= 8t-4pi.             (11)

At t<=1.860 the right side is 2.3136293856....

Likewise (6)-(9) give

    sum_r P_exc,r
      <= 40t_D D-20 per(F)+30nu+45x_B+40-10m-10d_tile.     (12)

At t_D<=1.860+o(1), this is at most

    (11.5681469282...+o(1))D.                               (13)

The decimals only evaluate proved coefficients; no numerical search is used.

## Remaining bottleneck

This does not close C-II. The allowance in (10) is still positive at the live
endpoint. A closure now needs either a lower bound on sum_r Q_r^+ + 2d_tile exceeding
(10), or a composition of the reduced exceptional-face allowance (12) with the
aggregate outer-walk/train obligations that yields a strict diameter decrease or
another canonical contradiction.

No verifier, CI result, or computational evidence is used.
